# Projective cocharacter limits and attracting points

Borel IV, 13.3 and 13.8: actual polynomial curves give highest-weight limits in
closed invariant projective sets. Finite fixed loci on connected closed orbits
force a one-dimensional highest part and a distinguished point with its exact
open basin. Character bounds and the two-point sign theorem connect these
limits to the centralizer-orbit orientation in 13.11–13.12; endpoint naturality
supports comparison of the original projective models.
-/
